{
  "_createdAt": "2026-04-27T21:32:49Z",
  "_id": "wp-post-115491-en",
  "_rev": "37hNSegHf4NtjSKr1qpn0Y",
  "_type": "article",
  "_updatedAt": "2026-07-05T16:12:28Z",
  "author": {
    "_ref": "author-legacy-archive",
    "_type": "reference"
  },
  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "000000000001",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000000",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt's beach holidays are not one kind."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000003",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "1lwh2h258nwm",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A Red Sea resort trip with pool, beach, kids' club, and snorkelling. A southward trip for coral reef and turtles. A trip with teenagers learning kitesurfing or diving. A trip from "
        },
        {
          "_key": "walohghrs4zp",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "jpaqtcw7b3bj"
          ],
          "text": "Cairo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "lgti4uz4e5hj",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " for one night by the sea. Or a Mediterranean trip at "
        },
        {
          "_key": "ej5ln3vaa7ai",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "nq0ff8z9p7vg"
          ],
          "text": "Alexandria"
        },
        {
          "_key": "tpbk6ryi4kyt",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " or "
        },
        {
          "_key": "wbhf8omtu3n7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "he78oybz49mz"
          ],
          "text": "Marsa Matruh"
        },
        {
          "_key": "rts7rjx50t3q",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "jpaqtcw7b3bj",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "nq0ff8z9p7vg",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58750",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "he78oybz49mz",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58887",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000005",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000004",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The same \"sea\" means very different things to a family."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000007",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "So the first thing to decide is not which beach is the prettiest. It is what your family needs — rest, marine life, resort convenience, city-and-sea combination."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000009",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Start with the Red Sea"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For families coming from abroad, the Red Sea is the most workable."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "qa5vjuho979i",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The reasons are clear. Clear water. Reef close by. Family-oriented resorts. Comparatively warm even in winter. Some areas combine well with Cairo or "
        },
        {
          "_key": "8rhisio4cqrc",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "8si2te0sc3l6"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor"
        },
        {
          "_key": "xehxwtnibm34",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "8si2te0sc3l6",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Family Red Sea resorts are quite practical. Private beach, multiple pools, shallow water, child-friendly food, kids' clubs, boat trips, snorkelling, dive centres. Placed in the second half of a trip, they restore children tired by sites."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000011",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000010",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Not every Red Sea beach suits toddlers. Some places have reef starting right off the shore, requiring a jetty to enter the water. Good for swimmers and snorkelling; inconvenient for small children playing in the shallows."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000013",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000012",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Confirm not the hotel's star rating but whether the beach is sandy, whether there is shallow water, whether it is jetty-based, whether reef is close, whether there is a lifeguard, whether there is a children's pool. This difference is large for family travel."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000015",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "hbmwkmjndx9x",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "vjoz3m11ya6c"
          ],
          "text": "Hurghada"
        },
        {
          "_key": "vvsy21opbc0k",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "r1uoqo6p3dsl",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "7eb047o1ydsp"
          ],
          "text": "El Gouna"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "vjoz3m11ya6c",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58859",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "7eb047o1ydsp",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58740",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000017",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For a first family beach, Hurghada and El Gouna are the easiest to combine."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000019",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000018",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hurghada is a big Red Sea resort city. Airport, many hotels, easy to combine with Luxor. Family-oriented all-inclusives, water-park hotels, snorkelling boat trips, and outings around the Giftun Islands are all there."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For convenience priority, Hurghada is strong. Families with small children, first-time Egypt families, and families resting after Cairo or Luxor find it easy. A region where hotel-choice failure is less likely."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hurghada is a resort city. Don't expect the air of a quiet fishing village. There are shops and a marina outside hotels, but the trip's centre is the hotel and the sea."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "El Gouna is more planned and calmer than Hurghada. Lagoons, marina, restaurants, and hotels are laid out, and walking or cycling is easy. Shallow lagoons suit small children; kitesurfing and similar water sports suit older children and teenagers."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000021",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For full-package all-inclusive comfort, Hurghada. For a town feel with room to step out in the evening, El Gouna. That split is practical."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000023",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Sharm el-Sheikh"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000025",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Sharm el-Sheikh is the international resort at the southern tip of Sinai."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000027",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "bkpc46o5ybw6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Family-oriented hotels, pools, beaches, boat trips, and dive centres are all there, with high completion as a Red Sea resort. The reefs at "
        },
        {
          "_key": "qzi6axuj2v0z",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "lla2j0b15imi"
          ],
          "text": "Ras Mohammed National Park"
        },
        {
          "_key": "24nua44n3pcl",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and the Strait of Tiran are major attractions for sea-focused families."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "lla2j0b15imi",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.sharm-el-sheikh.ras-mohammed-national-park",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000029",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000028",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For small children, the hotel beach conditions matter. Some Sharm beaches use jetties into deep water to protect coral. Good for fish-watching; not suited to toddlers playing in shallows. For sand and shallow water, confirm hotel-by-hotel."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For older children and teenagers, Sharm is strong. Snorkelling, beginner diving, boat trips, desert outings, possibly trips to St. Catherine's Monastery or Mount Sinai area."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Sinai areas can carry travel-advisory or insurance considerations depending on nationality and time. The Sharm resort area has long operated as a tourist destination; confirm current advice from your home country before booking."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "oqom2li7huak",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "s4ex3ifyhbwb"
          ],
          "text": "Marsa Alam"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "s4ex3ifyhbwb",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58885",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000031",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000030",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For sea priority, Marsa Alam is a candidate."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000033",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000032",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Quieter than Hurghada or Sharm, with southern Red Sea reef and wildlife as the appeal. Around Abu Dabbab and Marsa Mubarak, turtles and sometimes dugongs may be seen. Wild animals are not guaranteed; for families interested in marine life, very strong."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000035",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000034",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Marsa Alam suits children who can swim, who enjoy snorkelling, and who like sea creatures. Small children can enjoy it with the right hotel; overall, families with sea-ready children draw out more value."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000037",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000036",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Outside the resort, options are limited. The premise is spending time inside the hotel grounds. For families who want a different restaurant or town walk each night, El Gouna or Hurghada may fit better."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000039",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000038",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Consider access too. International and domestic flight schedules, airport-to-hotel distance, on-the-ground transfers. Marsa Alam is the place to pick when the sea leads."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "groa1oxsbh1n",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "nua1a7fevnij"
          ],
          "text": "Dahab"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "nua1a7fevnij",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-59436",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Dahab is a different Sinai sea from Sharm."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Less the world of a polished large resort, more a seaside town, dive shops, cafés, wind sports, and mountain views mixed. For families with older children and teenagers, a very interesting option."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000041",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000040",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The lagoon makes windsurfing and kitesurfing easy to learn, and the town's nearby reefs allow snorkelling. Desert and mountain day trips can be built in. Better for active sea stays than for passive resort holidays."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000043",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000042",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The famous Blue Hole is a strong dive site and known for depth-related risks. With families, handle it carefully — as surface snorkelling or as scenery. Deep diving is for experienced divers, not a children's playground."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000045",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000044",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Dahab may feel too free for families seeking fully managed resorts with young children. For families wanting a slightly independent trip with teenagers, it may stay in memory more than Sharm."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000047",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000046",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Ain Sokhna"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000049",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000048",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Ain Sokhna is the Red Sea close to Cairo."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Easy to drive from the capital, and used by Egyptian families heading to the sea on weekends. Convenient for adding one or two nights of beach to a Cairo stay."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "It is not where to expect the Red Sea's best reef or full resort experience. The value is closeness. A few days in Cairo, no extra domestic flights, with a little sea and pool time added for children. That is when it helps."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For a week-plus beach-centred family trip, Hurghada, El Gouna, Sharm, or Marsa Alam are the candidates."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000051",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000050",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Mediterranean coast"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000053",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000052",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt's Mediterranean is an entirely different trip from the Red Sea."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000055",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000054",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Alexandria is less a beach resort than a sea city. Corniche, the library, catacombs, fortress, cafés, Mediterranean air. With family, more natural to fit the sea into a city stay than to chase swimming."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000057",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000056",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Summer Alexandria crowds with domestic travellers. Beaches are also places of life; don't expect the polished quiet of an international resort. For older children, the city and history are interesting."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000059",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000058",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Marsa Matruh has particularly beautiful water on Egypt's Mediterranean. White sand, pale blue water, coves like Agiba Beach are very striking. The international family-resort base is less developed than the Red Sea. Suits families experienced with transfers, hotels, and local movement."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Mediterranean is less the place to reliably do a first family beach Egypt and more for an Egypt-experienced family wanting a different coast."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "How to choose by age"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "With toddlers and small children, prioritise shallow water, sandy beach, pool, child-friendly food, medical access, and being able to complete inside the hotel. Family resorts at El Gouna, Sahl Hasheesh, and Hurghada are easier."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000061",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000060",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For elementary-age children, snorkelling, boat trips, glass-bottom boats, and simple water sports fit in. Hurghada, Sharm, and El Gouna are candidates. With good swimmers, Marsa Alam appears too."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000063",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000062",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For teenagers, the trip widens. Discover Scuba, kitesurfing, windsurfing, the Sinai mountains, Marsa Alam wildlife, Dahab's independent atmosphere. Rather than parking kids at the hotel, choose experiences together."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000065",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000064",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For families with mixed ages, large resorts are easier. Pool and kids' club for the young; snorkelling and sports for older; rest time for adults. Don't try to give everyone the same experience."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000067",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000066",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Combining sites and sea"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000069",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000068",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In family travel, combining sites and sea makes Egypt work."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "ok07qzkxemil",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Two or three nights in Cairo and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "qmeriuq5o5hx",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "lroj4yllfggy"
          ],
          "text": "Giza"
        },
        {
          "_key": "r5f17kczfl50",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". Three or four on the Nile or Luxor. Three on the Red Sea. With ten to twelve days, this shape is very stable."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "lroj4yllfggy",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Put the sea at the end. Pyramids, museum, temples, and tombs first, then rest at the Red Sea. The children's stamina returns and adults close the trip calmly."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hurghada and El Gouna combine easily with Luxor. Drive from Luxor to the Red Sea, or arrange domestic flight or transfer."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000071",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000070",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Sharm suits trips that really enjoy the Sinai-side sea. Combined with Cairo or Luxor, confirm flight connections carefully."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000073",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000072",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Marsa Alam is excellent as a sea-led trip; combined with Nile sightseeing the transfer plan is harder."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000075",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000074",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Season"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000077",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000076",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Family Red Sea beach is easiest October to April. Not too hot, easy water entry. December to February has cool-air days and can be windy; resort stays remain comfortable."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000079",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000078",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Summer is hot, and seaside holidays still work. With pool and sea at the centre, it is much easier than summer Cairo or Luxor. July and August crowd in some areas with domestic and international holidays."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Mediterranean beaches are primarily summer. June to September. Winter Mediterranean is not a swimming destination."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For diving or snorkelling priority, factor Red Sea season, wind, water temperature, and children's swimming ability. Warm water doesn't mean every site suits beginners."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Safety and sea cautions"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000081",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000080",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For children in the water, confirm the hotel's beach conditions."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000083",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000082",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Shallow? Rocks or coral? Jetty entry? Lifeguard? Days with current from tide or wind? Are reef shoes needed? In family travel these are as important as room size."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000085",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000084",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Don't step on coral, don't touch it, don't feed fish. Use reef-safe sunscreen. Teach children that the Red Sea is a living sea, not a theme park."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000087",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000086",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Snorkelling, even with flotation, needs supervision. Strong swimmers can drift from shore. On boat trips, check life jackets, the guide's briefing, and the meeting point."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000089",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000088",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For Discover Scuba, use a certified centre. Confirm age limits, health, insurance, and instructor ratios. Don't choose on price alone."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Which to pick"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Convenient, low-failure family beach: Hurghada."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Slightly polished town feel with shallow lagoons: El Gouna."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000091",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000090",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "International resort with strong reef: Sharm el-Sheikh."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000093",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000092",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Marine life and quiet: Marsa Alam."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000095",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000094",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Active time with teenagers: Dahab."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000097",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000096",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A short sea close to Cairo: Ain Sokhna."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000099",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000098",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "City-and-Mediterranean combination: Alexandria."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000009b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000009a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egyptian summer sea with beautiful water: Marsa Matruh."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000009d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000009c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "No single right answer. Children's ages, swimming ability, trip length, combination with sites, and whether you want to complete inside the hotel — all shift the answer."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000009f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000009e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Egyptian sea is not just a place to rest after the pyramids."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000a1",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000a0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In family travel, the sea balances the whole trip. It absorbs the weight of history, restores children's stamina, and gives quiet time to adults."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000a3",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000a2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "So when choosing a family beach in Egypt, don't decide on view alone."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "0000000000a5",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "0000000000a4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Decide by how that sea will work inside your family's day."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    }
  ],
